# Tech Stack - feature/database (Maddi Soumya)

Database Engine : PostgreSQL (local server install; not a cloud service)
Setup Tooling   : node-postgres (`pg` npm package) - pure JavaScript
                  wire-protocol client used only by the bootstrap
                  scripts in database/ (migrate/seed/reset/verify), not
                  the application's runtime data layer, which is
                  Python/FastAPI + SQLAlchemy per docs/spec.md
Schema          : Plain SQL DDL file (database/schema.sql) using UUID
                  primary keys (gen_random_uuid(), built into Postgres
                  core since v13), native ENUM types, DATE/TIMESTAMPTZ,
                  and NUMERIC for exact-precision money math
Seed Data       : Plain SQL INSERT statements (database/seed.sql) with
                  fixed, readable UUID literals - not static JSON
Tooling scripts : database/migrate.js (creates db + applies schema.sql),
                  database/seed.js (applies seed.sql),
                  database/reset.js (migrate + seed in one step),
                  database/verify.js (row-count + business-rule checks)
Config          : .env (git-ignored, per-developer) + config.js, using
                  standard PGHOST/PGPORT/PGUSER/PGPASSWORD/PGDATABASE
                  environment variables

Naming/shape note: this schema was rewritten once already to match the
team-agreed conventions in status.md and docs/modules/*.md (UUID ids,
employees.name instead of first/last name, department/job_position as
plain text instead of separate tables, contract date_start/date_end,
contract status "active" not "running", allocations/schedule_lines
table names, payslip warnings as a JSONB column, etc.). If a name here
looks unusual, check those docs first - it's intentional, not a typo.

Why this stack:
- Full relational database engine with native enum types, exact-numeric
  money columns, and constraints/triggers enforced by the server itself.
- Still fully local - runs on a PostgreSQL server installed on your own
  machine, no cloud database account required.
- No native build tooling needed to install the setup driver (pg is
  pure JS), unlike better-sqlite3 which failed to build on this machine
  due to a missing Visual Studio toolchain.
- schema.sql/seed.sql are plain SQL, so they double as init scripts the
  official postgres Docker image can run automatically (NFR-06) and
  can be applied with plain `psql` if someone doesn't want Node at all.
- A real, dynamic, queryable relational database (not static JSON),
  satisfying the "use real-time/dynamic data sources" requirement.

Where things live:
  PeoplePay360_Team301/database/
    schema.sql   - full DDL: users, employees, working schedules,
                   schedule lines, contracts (period-aware, with
                   overlap-prevention trigger), attendance, time off
                   types/allocations/requests, salary structures/rules,
                   payruns/payrun_employees/payslips/payslip lines
    seed.sql     - demo data reproducing the README's worked examples
                   (contract resolution, leave balance flow)
    migrate.js   - creates the database (if missing) and applies schema.sql
    seed.js      - applies seed.sql
    reset.js     - one-shot: migrate + seed
    verify.js    - prints row counts and checks key business rules
    config.js    - loads .env and centralizes PG connection config
    errors.js    - unwraps pg/Node connection errors into a readable message
    .env.example - template for local Postgres connection credentials
    README.md    - setup + usage instructions for the rest of the team

Prerequisite (not committed to the repo): a running local PostgreSQL
server. Install from https://www.postgresql.org/download/ - any
version 13+ works. See database/README.md for full setup steps.
